  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - The London Borough of Hounslow as the Local Planning Authority hereby certifies that on 19th March 2007, the erection of a single storey rear/side infill extension, with dimensions 1.70 metres wide, 5.20 metres deep, and 2.80 metres high, returning a volume of 25.06m3, giving a total volume increase to the original house of 49.23m3, as shown on drawing number 946/01B, received 19 March 2007, was lawful within the meaning of Section 191 and 192 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 for the following reason:\r\nFollowing the proposed extensions consisting of the erection of a single storey rear/side infill extension, the resulting building would fall within the provisions of Schedule 2, Part 1, Class A of the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) Order 1995.\r\n"
